# Backend Architecture Rules

## File Placement

| What | Where | Never Put It |
|------|-------|-------------|
| HTTP routes | `app/api/v1/{module}/` | services/, repositories/ |
| Business logic | `app/services/{module}/` | api/, repositories/, workers/ |
| Event publishing | `app/events/` | services/ (inline worker.delay) |
| DB queries | `app/repositories/` | api/, services/ (directly) |
| Beanie models | `app/models/` | schemas/ |
| Request/response DTOs | `app/schemas/` | models/ |
| Celery tasks | `app/workers/` | services/ (inline) |
| LLM calls | `app/ai/` | services/ (direct ollama), repositories/ |
| Job scrapers | `app/collectors/` | services/, workers/ (logic) |
| Cron triggers | `app/scheduler/` | workers/ (cron defs) |

## API Router Pattern

```python
# api/v1/resumes/router.py
@router.post("/upload")
async def upload_resume(
    file: UploadFile,
    current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user),
    service: ResumeService = Depends(get_resume_service),
) -> ResumeResponse:
    return await service.upload(current_user.id, file)
```

## Service Pattern

```python
# services/application/application_service.py
class ApplicationService:
    async def apply(self, application_id: str, user_id: str) -> ApplicationResponse:
        # validate, persist
        await self.history_repo.log(application_id, "apply_requested")
        publish_application_submitted(application_id, user_id)  # events/, NOT worker.delay()
        return ApplicationResponse(...)
```

## Do NOT

- Import Beanie models in API layer (use schemas)
- Call Ollama directly from services (use `app/ai/`)
- Call `worker.delay()` from services (use `app/events/`)
- Put parsing logic in services (belongs in `resume_parser` worker)
- Put scraping in scheduler (belongs in `job_scraper` worker)
